#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:32
msgid "Welcome to OTPClient"
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:33
msgid ""
"A secure authenticator for TOTP and HOTP tokens.\n"
"\n"
"Your tokens are stored in encrypted databases protected by a master password."
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:39
msgid "OTPs Are Hidden by Default"
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:40
msgid ""
"Codes are hidden in the list to prevent shoulder-surfing and accidental "
"screenshot leaks.\n"
"\n"
"Selecting a row does not reveal or copy anything. Use the row's Copy button, "
"double-click the row, or press Enter or Ctrl+C on the selected token, and "
"the code is copied and briefly shown so you can check it. HOTP rows have a "
"Generate button instead, because producing a code consumes a counter.\n"
"\n"
"Turn this off in Settings -> Display to keep TOTP codes visible at all times."
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:52
msgid "Multiple Databases"
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:53
msgid ""
"You can create and manage multiple encrypted databases from the sidebar.\n"
"\n"
"The first database you create becomes the default - it loads automatically "
"on startup and is marked with a star. The currently open database is shown "
"in bold.\n"
"\n"
"Right-click a database to rename it, set it as the default, or remove it "
"from the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:63
msgid "Organize with Groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:64
msgid ""
"Organize your tokens into groups for quick filtering.\n"
"\n"
"Use the dropdown in the header bar to filter by group, or search with the "
"“group:” prefix. Assign groups by right-clicking a token."
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:71
msgid "Keyboard Shortcuts & Search"
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:72
msgid ""
"Use Ctrl+N to add a token, Ctrl+F to search, F2 to edit, and Ctrl+? to see "
"all shortcuts.\n"
"\n"
"Desktop search integration lets you find tokens from GNOME or KDE without "
"opening the app."
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:80
msgid ""
"Secret Service integration can store your database password in the system "
"keyring so the app unlocks automatically after login. It is disabled by "
"default.\n"
"\n"
"You can enable it and configure auto-lock in Settings -> Security."
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:87
msgid "Settings & Backup"
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:88
msgid ""
"All preferences are in the Settings dialog, including countdown colors and "
"clipboard auto-clear.\n"
"\n"
"Back up and restore both your application preferences and your token "
"database from Settings -> Backup, or via the CLI with --export-settings and "
"--import-settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:101
msgid "Tokens That Need Repair"
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:102
msgid ""
"A token the app cannot accept, such as one with an out-of-range digit count, "
"is set aside so the rest of the database still opens. It used to get a "
"single toast and nothing more.\n"
"\n"
"A banner now counts those tokens, and Review lets you repair or delete each "
"one. A repair is validated before it replaces the preserved copy, and a "
"failed repair changes nothing. Deleting asks first and cannot be undone, "
"because the preserved token may be the only copy of its secret."
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:113
msgid "Select Several Tokens"
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:114
msgid ""
"Choose Select in the header bar to show a checkbox on every row. Checked "
"tokens can be assigned to a group, exported, or deleted, and a bulk delete "
"can be undone from its toast.\n"
"\n"
"Only checked tokens you can see are affected: changing the search or the "
"group filter unchecks the ones it hides. Tokens from other databases that "
"appear in search results are read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:125
msgid ""
"Manage Groups, in the main menu, renames a group across all its tokens at "
"once, or removes the group from them. The tokens themselves are kept.\n"
"\n"
"Searching with the “group:” prefix now matches every group whose name "
"contains the text, so group:wo finds Work and Workshop alike. When nothing "
"matches, Clear Filters resets the search and the group."
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:135
msgid "Preview Before Importing"
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:136
msgid ""
"Choosing a file now lists what it contains before anything is added. Exact "
"duplicates are unchecked and skipped. A token with the same issuer and "
"account but a different secret is flagged, so you can decide whether it "
"replaces the old one or is a second account.\n"
"\n"
"Uncheck anything you do not want, then choose Import Selected. Entries the "
"source file could not provide are listed with the reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:147
msgid "Work Stays in the Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../src/gui/dialogs/whats-new-dialog.c:148
msgid ""
"Reading a backup, writing an export, and changing the database password or "
"key-derivation settings no longer freeze the window while they run.\n"
"\n"
"While a password or key-derivation change runs, the token actions are "
"disabled, and the app stays open until it finishes. A password change "
"reports how it ended, and one that finishes after the app has locked still "
"updates the system keyring."
msgstr ""

